  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1218 PM MST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nTemperatures will continue to warm a degree or two across eastern\nNM on Tuesday as a weak lee side trough and downslope winds\ndevelop. Apart from a few breezes around KCQC, should be another\nbeautiful day. A shortwave trough will slide over the central\nRockies Tuesday and dive southeastward toward Oklahoma on\nWednesday. An associated cold front will back into NM Tuesday\nnight and Wednesday, bringing breezy winds and slightly cooler \ntemperatures. A gap wind may be noted below gaps of the Central\nMtn Chain Wednesday, particularly across the lower Rio Grande \nValley as well as the upper Tularosa Valley.\n\nA weak reinforcing front may arrive on Thursday as another\nshortwave slides southward across the Upper Midwest, but upper \nlevel ridging will be moving toward NM from the west. This \nridging will cross the state on Friday. Thus, quiet conditions \npersist Thursday and Friday with near to above normal temperatures\nand light winds.\n\nAfter the ridge shifts eastward, all eyes will be on an upper\nlevel low racing toward the northern Baja. The low is expected to\nweaken into an open wave as it shifts northeastward over NM this\nweekend. Since the low will be weakening, and it will shift across\nNM rather quickly, not looking for large precipitation amounts.\nThere will be enough moisture for rain showers and very high\nelevation snow showers, but thunderstorms are unlikely. Western\nand southern portions of the CWA will be favored for light\nprecipitation, mainly from Saturday afternoon through early\nSunday.",
